      "problem": "Solve the equation $2\\cdot 3^x=54.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we divide both sides of the equation by $2\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot {3}^{x} & =54 \\\\ \\frac{2\\cdot {3}^{x}}{2} & =\\frac{54}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{2}\\cdot {3}^{x}}{\\cancel{2}} & =27 \\\\ {3}^{x} & =27\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite $27$ as $3^3$ so that both sides have the same base:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3}^{x}={3}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the exponents, we get ${\\color{blue}x}={\\color{blue}3}.$",
